WEBVTT

1
00:01:21.197 --> 00:01:22.977
Guess you don't remember me.

2
00:01:23.057 --> 00:01:24.577
Can't say you do.

3
00:01:24.797 --> 00:01:27.137
Yet there's something
mighty familiar about you.

4
00:01:27.217 --> 00:01:30.937
Well, Jake, I guess it's a long time since
you taught me how to trap coyotes and

5
00:01:31.017 --> 00:01:34.117
ride rocks. Jerry Mason as I live.

6
00:01:34.197 --> 00:01:37.217
Well, well, man, how you've grown.

7
00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:39.537
Why, say, you're a regular
mountain, ain't you?

8
00:01:39.617 --> 00:01:42.177
Ha, sit down here and let's talk it over.

9
00:01:42.637 --> 00:01:44.937
Well, there's not much to tell, Jake.

10
00:01:45.017 --> 00:01:49.097
Finished college and true to your dad's
last request, you've come to live with me,

11
00:01:49.177 --> 00:01:49.857
eh?

12
00:01:49.937 --> 00:01:51.117
That's right.

13
00:01:51.197 --> 00:01:53.457
I can't tell you how
happy I am seeing you.

14
00:01:53.537 --> 00:01:55.713
Well, I'm happy to be here too, Jake.

15
00:01:56.277 --> 00:01:58.577
How about the ranch? Cattle?

16
00:01:59.057 --> 00:02:00.657
There ain't no cattle, son.

17
00:02:01.177 --> 00:02:04.118
Rustler's got most of them,
and I sold those left.

18
00:02:04.477 --> 00:02:06.497
Can we stock it up again?

19
00:02:06.677 --> 00:02:08.559
Or starting some other business?

20
00:02:08.817 --> 00:02:10.557
Itching to get to work, eh?

21
00:02:11.157 --> 00:02:16.157
Well, I was figuring on opening
up the blacksmith shop, but...

22
00:02:18.197 --> 00:02:21.817
What do you say we go in and fry us
the chicken and gargle some coffee?

23
00:02:21.897 --> 00:02:26.015
What do you say, huh? Sounds like
a good idea, especially the chicken.

24
00:02:37.037 --> 00:02:39.877
Well, no wonder this horse was limping.

25
00:03:05.297 --> 00:03:06.757
Well, got him fixed up.

26
00:03:06.837 --> 00:03:07.837
Yep.

27
00:03:08.317 --> 00:03:09.977
All spicked up a sharp rock.

28
00:03:10.057 --> 00:03:11.857
No, no, there ain't no charge.

29
00:03:12.217 --> 00:03:14.257
Looks like you've been
through plenty of water.

30
00:03:14.337 --> 00:03:17.797
Oh, yeah, tried a shortcut about 12
miles back down there and got stuck.

31
00:03:17.877 --> 00:03:19.997
Oh, come right down through
the middle of the creek.

32
00:03:20.077 --> 00:03:21.077
Hmm.

33
00:03:21.317 --> 00:03:22.297
That's where he went lame.

34
00:03:22.377 --> 00:03:23.377
Well,

35
00:03:23.677 --> 00:03:24.817
good luck to you.

36
00:03:38.457 --> 00:03:39.897
Hey, Jake.

37
00:03:41.877 --> 00:03:44.417
I just picked this up at the post office.

38
00:03:45.257 --> 00:03:47.217
I bet I know who it's from.

39
00:03:48.037 --> 00:03:49.597
I was right.

40
00:03:49.897 --> 00:03:51.397
It's from Betty.

41
00:03:59.137 --> 00:04:00.577
Well, I was right.

42
00:04:00.657 --> 00:04:01.957
It's from Betty.

43
00:04:02.037 --> 00:04:04.637
Betty? Yeah, my granddaughter.

44
00:04:05.297 --> 00:04:06.417
Did you know I had granddaughter?

45
00:04:06.497 --> 00:04:07.817
I certainly did not.

46
00:04:07.897 --> 00:04:09.397
Yes, sirree.

47
00:04:09.477 --> 00:04:11.217
I'm her only living relative.

48
00:04:11.477 --> 00:04:13.917
I've been sent her to
college for a couple of years.

49
00:04:13.997 --> 00:04:16.197
But she'll soon be here to live with me.

50
00:04:16.277 --> 00:04:18.159
Let's see what she's got to say.

51
00:04:28.697 --> 00:04:34.597
Dear Grandy, I just received my
monthly check and thank you so much.

52
00:04:35.297 --> 00:04:39.197
I can't wait until school is over
so I can come and live with you.

53
00:04:39.277 --> 00:04:43.857
Gee, just three months more and
I'll be keeping house for you.

54
00:04:43.937 --> 00:04:47.477
Please write me a nice long letter.

55
00:04:47.557 --> 00:04:50.977
I do so enjoy hearing from you.

56
00:04:51.277 --> 00:04:52.757
Lovingly Betty.

57
00:04:54.557 --> 00:04:56.877
She's a fine girl, Jerry.

58
00:04:57.037 --> 00:05:01.237
And I'm gonna do everything
I can to make her happy.

59
00:05:04.857 --> 00:05:06.797
Well, hello, Freddy.

60
00:05:09.677 --> 00:05:12.377
She's a town dog. Everybody feeds her.

61
00:05:27.597 --> 00:05:30.197
Oh, so you want to play, eh?

62
00:05:31.817 --> 00:05:33.077
Say, Jake.

63
00:05:33.537 --> 00:05:34.517
Take a look.

64
00:05:34.597 --> 00:05:37.337
That's that piece of quartz that
came out of the horse's hook.

65
00:05:37.417 --> 00:05:38.657
It's gold.

66
00:05:40.017 --> 00:05:43.605
Say, there's a stringer in there
bigger than a tenpenny nail.

67
00:05:43.797 --> 00:05:45.637
We only knew where it came from.

68
00:05:45.717 --> 00:05:46.977
I do know.

69
00:05:47.177 --> 00:05:50.937
That prospector said he was forced down
the middle of a creek twelve miles out.

70
00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:55.297
Well, there's only one creek out there,
Jerry, and it'll be a cinch to backtrack it.

71
00:05:55.377 --> 00:05:58.137
Well, we're on our way right
now, and if we find anything,

72
00:05:58.217 --> 00:06:02.117
I know a dog that's gonna have a
porterhouse steak and a home for life.

73
00:06:02.197 --> 00:06:03.597
You said it.

74
00:06:22.077 --> 00:06:24.312
Right there's where he left the creek.

75
00:06:30.677 --> 00:06:32.617
Thank you.

76
00:07:08.777 --> 00:07:11.017
Hey, that's the real stuff, son.

77
00:07:11.397 --> 00:07:14.338
According to this sand,
the creek's full of color.

78
00:07:29.057 --> 00:07:29.757
Hello.

79
00:07:29.837 --> 00:07:31.657
Hello, Benson. What can I do for you?

80
00:07:31.737 --> 00:07:33.737
In first place, do you fellas buy gold?

81
00:07:33.817 --> 00:07:36.111
Certainly. That's part of our business.

82
00:07:36.517 --> 00:07:37.817
I'll see what we got.

83
00:07:43.617 --> 00:07:46.157
Say, that's the purest stuff.

84
00:07:46.397 --> 00:07:48.277
Good as I've ever seen.

85
00:07:52.297 --> 00:07:54.597
They've made a great strike somewhere.

86
00:08:12.617 --> 00:08:13.997
Let's see.

87
00:08:14.777 --> 00:08:17.237
At $16 an ounce,

88
00:08:18.497 --> 00:08:21.017
that'll come to $848.

89
00:08:22.597 --> 00:08:26.303
Okay, we'll take that in currency
if it's just the same to you.

90
00:08:26.457 --> 00:08:28.217
Okay, all right, Joe.

91
00:08:29.437 --> 00:08:30.617
Now listen.

92
00:08:30.697 --> 00:08:33.297
We expect to bring in
many times that amount.

93
00:08:33.377 --> 00:08:35.357
We think we've got a rich strike.

94
00:08:36.517 --> 00:08:38.137
to know anything about it.

95
00:08:38.217 --> 00:08:39.637
But you'll tell us, won't you?

96
00:08:39.717 --> 00:08:41.697
We're not telling anybody, Harris.

97
00:08:41.777 --> 00:08:45.857
But when we do get ready to let the location
be known, you'll be the first ones in

98
00:08:45.937 --> 00:08:47.637
on it. Thanks. Come on, Jake.

99
00:08:47.717 --> 00:08:50.129
We gotta go buy a dog a porterhouse date.

100
00:08:52.337 --> 00:08:55.777
They made a rich strike,
and it's up to us to locate it.

101
00:08:56.237 --> 00:08:59.737
I wouldn't mind having old
man Benson's ranch, either.

102
00:09:00.837 --> 00:09:02.817
He used to run cattle.

103
00:09:04.317 --> 00:09:08.717
Of course, he doesn't know
it, but I got most of them.

104
00:09:32.417 --> 00:09:36.123
You know, Jake, it's a good thing
we didn't file on that claim.

105
00:09:37.117 --> 00:09:42.017
It had tipped the whole town off to the
location and confined our operations.

106
00:09:42.437 --> 00:09:44.177
As it is, we can work the whole creek.

107
00:09:44.257 --> 00:09:45.257
Yeah.

108
00:09:45.657 --> 00:09:49.757
Your idea of crossing Windy Flats and
entering the town from the other side sure had

109
00:09:49.837 --> 00:09:50.857
them puzzled.

110
00:09:51.137 --> 00:09:52.797
It sure has.

111
00:09:52.877 --> 00:09:56.957
They've been back trailing us now for two
months, and they always get stuck at Windy

112
00:09:57.037 --> 00:09:57.857
Flats.

113
00:09:57.937 --> 00:10:00.517
They think this mine's out
in the middle of the desert.

114
00:10:00.597 --> 00:10:02.773
Why don't we take a little rest, son?

115
00:10:04.337 --> 00:10:07.217
Just a few more days
and Betty will be coming.

116
00:10:09.257 --> 00:10:11.097
Well, don't you think we'd
better be getting back...

117
00:10:11.177 --> 00:10:12.777
...and getting some of
this dirt out of our hide?

118
00:10:12.857 --> 00:10:15.077
Yeah, I reckon you're right.

119
00:10:15.277 --> 00:10:16.277
You know,

120
00:10:16.437 --> 00:10:18.557
you want to sure look your best.

121
00:10:36.937 --> 00:10:38.177
Well, well.

122
00:10:38.257 --> 00:10:40.397
Hello, Hank. How's your old woman?

123
00:10:40.477 --> 00:10:42.377
What's next? What do you got now?

124
00:10:42.457 --> 00:10:44.557
It's all washed up, boys.

125
00:10:44.637 --> 00:10:46.257
No pay dirt this time.

126
00:10:46.337 --> 00:10:47.497
Oh, come on.

127
00:10:49.397 --> 00:10:51.617
Hey, wait a minute. Wait a minute.

128
00:10:51.697 --> 00:10:54.037
I tell you, we didn't get a bit of color.

129
00:10:54.117 --> 00:10:58.657
Oh, boy. How about we didn't go all
this time and not a bit of color?

130
00:10:59.457 --> 00:11:00.777
Hold on. Now, wait a minute.

131
00:11:00.857 --> 00:11:02.210
Tell you what it'll do.

132
00:11:02.317 --> 00:11:05.157
I'll give you every nugget
you find in the past.

133
00:11:05.517 --> 00:11:08.457
Yeah, go on ahead and search it.

134
00:11:12.617 --> 00:11:15.497
Here comes old Benson now,
and Mason isn't with him.

135
00:11:15.577 --> 00:11:17.617
Good. Are the papers all ready?

136
00:11:17.697 --> 00:11:18.737
Everything.

137
00:11:23.137 --> 00:11:25.057
Hello, Jake. Hello, Benson.

138
00:11:25.437 --> 00:11:27.057
Well, what luck this time?

139
00:11:27.137 --> 00:11:28.377
Not so bad.

140
00:11:28.537 --> 00:11:30.317
Not so bad.

141
00:11:56.597 --> 00:11:59.317
That looks kind of official to me.

142
00:12:03.597 --> 00:12:06.377
Let's see. It's $16 an ounce.

143
00:12:06.457 --> 00:12:08.257
That's, uh...

144
00:12:08.337 --> 00:12:10.837
$2,335.

145
00:12:11.297 --> 00:12:13.177
How do you have it, in coin or bills?

146
00:12:13.257 --> 00:12:15.357
Well, bills is easier to carry.

147
00:12:15.597 --> 00:12:16.757
All right, Joe.

148
00:12:17.597 --> 00:12:19.137
Sit down, Jake.

149
00:12:24.537 --> 00:12:26.837
I've got to have your
signature this time, Jake.

150
00:12:26.917 --> 00:12:30.517
The government demands that they get a
receipt for all monies paid out for raw gold.

151
00:12:30.597 --> 00:12:31.597
Sure.

152
00:12:34.057 --> 00:12:35.137
But, Joe,

153
00:12:36.957 --> 00:12:38.898
stamp the date on that, will you?

154
00:12:46.377 --> 00:12:47.637
I'm sorry.

155
00:12:50.777 --> 00:12:52.717
Thank you.

156
00:13:27.197 --> 00:13:28.317
There you are.

157
00:13:28.397 --> 00:13:30.177
And here's your money. Thanks.

158
00:13:30.257 --> 00:13:31.963
Give him a canteen, will you?

159
00:13:32.637 --> 00:13:35.517
I'll be seeing you
fellas again mighty soon.

160
00:13:35.657 --> 00:13:36.657
Goodbye.

161
00:13:42.617 --> 00:13:47.057
Well, we got the deed to the ranch,
and when he eventually disappears,

162
00:13:47.137 --> 00:13:48.677
we'll have this recorded.

163
00:13:49.377 --> 00:13:51.612
Let's see what we made on the nuggets.

164
00:13:55.617 --> 00:13:57.677
Well, how much do we get this time?

165
00:13:57.757 --> 00:14:00.297
$2,335.

166
00:14:00.377 --> 00:14:01.377
Whoo!

167
00:14:01.737 --> 00:14:04.137
I'm gonna hold out $500 of that.

168
00:14:04.217 --> 00:14:06.617
Pay on this blacksmith shop tomorrow.

169
00:14:07.577 --> 00:14:08.837
You know, Jerry,

170
00:14:09.097 --> 00:14:13.157
I got an idea this is gonna
be a valuable corner someday.

171
00:14:13.917 --> 00:14:16.477
And we ain't gonna let go of it.

172
00:14:17.557 --> 00:14:19.637
I think it's a good investment, Jake.

173
00:14:19.717 --> 00:14:20.317
I think it's a good investment, Jake.

174
00:14:20.397 --> 00:14:22.221
I think it's a good investment.

175
00:14:29.537 --> 00:14:30.797
Hello, Dad.

176
00:14:31.377 --> 00:14:33.848
Say, you got a couple bucks you can spare?

177
00:14:34.597 --> 00:14:35.877
Gambling again, eh?

178
00:14:35.957 --> 00:14:38.917
Well, that's about all there
is to do around this town.

179
00:14:38.997 --> 00:14:40.657
Gee, I wish I had a job.

180
00:14:41.257 --> 00:14:42.497
So do I.

181
00:14:43.157 --> 00:14:44.377
And remember...

182
00:14:44.477 --> 00:14:46.317
you can't keep this up forever.

183
00:14:46.397 --> 00:14:48.103
There's an end to everything.

184
00:14:58.417 --> 00:14:59.497
Hey, Al.

185
00:14:59.717 --> 00:15:00.937
Come here a minute.

186
00:15:02.397 --> 00:15:06.077
If you don't kick through that dough you
owe me, I'm telling the town everything.

187
00:15:06.157 --> 00:15:08.777
That'll just about throw
your old man out of office.

188
00:15:08.857 --> 00:15:09.977
Where am I going to get it?

189
00:15:10.057 --> 00:15:12.917
That's not up to me. I don't care
where you get it or how you get it,

190
00:15:12.997 --> 00:15:13.997
but get it.

191
00:15:46.297 --> 00:15:48.197
Mr. Williams in? Yes, Jake.

192
00:15:48.277 --> 00:15:49.317
You'll find him in his office.

193
00:15:49.397 --> 00:15:50.397
Thanks.

194
00:15:52.497 --> 00:15:53.577
Come in.

195
00:15:58.317 --> 00:15:59.517
Hi, Mr. Williams.

196
00:15:59.597 --> 00:16:00.977
Hi, Nick. I'm glad to see you.

197
00:16:01.057 --> 00:16:03.997
I want to pay off my debt
on the Lexington shop.

198
00:16:04.077 --> 00:16:05.477
Well, that's fine.

199
00:16:05.737 --> 00:16:06.677
Sit down.

200
00:16:06.757 --> 00:16:08.037
Thank you, sir.

201
00:16:18.837 --> 00:16:21.131
I'll give you a receipt for your money.

202
00:16:22.157 --> 00:16:23.897
You'll put it into escrow.

203
00:16:24.897 --> 00:16:26.956
You'll get your deed in a few days.

204
00:16:45.597 --> 00:16:47.097
All right, Miss Williams.

205
00:16:47.277 --> 00:16:48.677
How's the plane coming?

206
00:16:48.757 --> 00:16:51.357
Oh, still coughing up a few colors.

207
00:16:51.797 --> 00:16:54.856
Won't be working it again
until next spring, though.

208
00:16:55.297 --> 00:16:56.297
Oh,

209
00:16:57.677 --> 00:16:59.383
let's go. Let's go. Let's go.

210
00:17:01.057 --> 00:17:02.237
Howdy, Sheriff.

211
00:17:02.317 --> 00:17:03.757
Hello, Indian.

212
00:17:36.397 --> 00:17:38.750
You better send for the doctor, Sheriff.

213
00:17:44.197 --> 00:17:45.497
It's too late.

214
00:17:46.057 --> 00:17:47.477
You've killed him, Jake.

215
00:17:49.257 --> 00:17:50.537
I killed him?

216
00:17:50.617 --> 00:17:52.497
You're not trying to deny it, are you?

217
00:17:52.577 --> 00:17:53.957
Didn't I hear you fighting?

218
00:17:54.037 --> 00:17:55.437
You were the only one in here, Mr.

219
00:17:55.517 --> 00:17:56.517
Benson.

220
00:18:04.857 --> 00:18:07.677
Somebody must have come
in through the back door.

221
00:18:07.757 --> 00:18:09.637
That's the only way
it could have happened.

222
00:18:09.717 --> 00:18:11.337
Don't worry, old-timer.

223
00:18:11.417 --> 00:18:13.770
I'll have you out of here in North Town.

224
00:18:44.557 --> 00:18:46.817
This is Mr. Benson's ranch, isn't it?

225
00:18:46.897 --> 00:18:47.817
Why, yes.

226
00:18:47.897 --> 00:18:48.977
Are you Betty?

227
00:18:50.157 --> 00:18:51.517
And you're Jerry Mason.

228
00:18:51.597 --> 00:18:53.977
Well, why didn't you let us
know you were coming today?

229
00:18:54.057 --> 00:18:56.137
Yeah, I wanted a surprise, Grandy.

230
00:18:56.617 --> 00:18:57.997
Why, where is he?

231
00:18:58.677 --> 00:18:59.917
Oh, uh,

232
00:19:00.577 --> 00:19:04.277
well, uh, you see, when he gets
out in the hills prospecting,

233
00:19:04.357 --> 00:19:08.357
why, uh, he's Well, it's pretty
hard to tell when he is coming back.

234
00:19:09.497 --> 00:19:10.777
Won't you come in?

235
00:19:12.357 --> 00:19:15.517
Oh, gee, you don't know
how glad I am to be here.

236
00:19:15.597 --> 00:19:17.977
But I just can't wait to see Grandy.

237
00:19:18.057 --> 00:19:20.377
Well, I'm going to ride out
and see if I can locate him.

238
00:19:20.457 --> 00:19:22.177
Oh, I hope you find him.

239
00:19:28.777 --> 00:19:31.197
Now, just make yourself
comfortable, Miss Betty.

240
00:19:31.277 --> 00:19:34.777
Well, thank you. And I have dinner
ready for you when you come back.

241
00:19:34.857 --> 00:19:36.657
That'll be great. Goodbye.

242
00:19:36.737 --> 00:19:37.737
Goodbye.

243
00:20:02.977 --> 00:20:04.937
Is there any news, Jerry?

244
00:20:05.317 --> 00:20:06.317
Nope.

245
00:20:06.697 --> 00:20:09.077
I'm just going to give
this bank the once over.

246
00:20:09.157 --> 00:20:13.397
Well, this may not mean anything,
but Al, the sheriff's son,

247
00:20:13.477 --> 00:20:15.517
has been flashing a roll of bills.

248
00:20:15.597 --> 00:20:18.362
Now, I know he hasn't
done anything to earn it.

249
00:20:18.617 --> 00:20:22.037
He just paid me for a horse I sold him.

250
00:20:27.777 --> 00:20:29.837
Did Al Miller give you this money?

251
00:20:29.917 --> 00:20:31.377
He sure did.

252
00:20:39.077 --> 00:20:41.097
Where'd you get that money, Miller?

253
00:20:41.177 --> 00:20:43.037
Why, I don't think that's
none of your business.

254
00:20:43.117 --> 00:20:46.077
Well, I'm making it my business because
that's part of the money Jake Benson paid

255
00:20:46.157 --> 00:20:46.897
the banker.

256
00:20:46.977 --> 00:20:48.457
Now, just wait if you get it.

257
00:20:48.537 --> 00:20:51.577
As I told you before,
it's none of your business.

258
00:21:23.577 --> 00:21:26.877
Come on!

259
00:21:51.437 --> 00:21:54.737
Come on!

260
00:22:15.997 --> 00:22:17.357
Come on, Lillard.

261
00:22:17.437 --> 00:22:18.437
Come on,

262
00:22:29.557 --> 00:22:30.557
Lillard.

263
00:22:31.197 --> 00:22:33.297
Tell these boys where you got that money.

264
00:22:33.377 --> 00:22:34.597
None of your business.

265
00:22:34.677 --> 00:22:35.817
Oh, no.

266
00:22:36.337 --> 00:22:38.057
I did it. I did it.

267
00:22:38.137 --> 00:22:39.157
Let me go.

268
00:22:39.637 --> 00:22:40.797
You hear that, boys?

269
00:22:40.877 --> 00:22:41.597
Yeah.

270
00:22:41.677 --> 00:22:43.377
I hear you. I hear you.

271
00:22:45.337 --> 00:22:46.757
Get there!

272
00:22:47.437 --> 00:22:48.597
Shut up!

273
00:22:49.157 --> 00:22:50.977
Why are you gonna stay
right now, this boy?

274
00:22:51.057 --> 00:22:52.017
Get the chair!

275
00:22:52.097 --> 00:22:53.937
Watch that one, get away!

276
00:22:55.617 --> 00:22:56.877
Let it go!

277
00:22:56.957 --> 00:22:58.137
Get it!

278
00:23:29.097 --> 00:23:31.297
He's got the best horse.

279
00:24:11.917 --> 00:24:12.917
Oh, my God.

280
00:25:05.377 --> 00:25:08.117
I said you, sheriff, Jake is innocent.

281
00:25:09.537 --> 00:25:10.997
Wait a minute, then.

282
00:25:11.737 --> 00:25:15.997
If what you say is true, and
my boy is guilty of this crime,

283
00:25:16.077 --> 00:25:19.037
I'll see that he gets the
full penalty of the law.

284
00:25:19.297 --> 00:25:20.597
So here comes Mason, now.

285
00:25:20.677 --> 00:25:22.177
Yeah, there he comes.

286
00:25:36.017 --> 00:25:40.277
Howton Miller, I arrest you for
attempted murder and robbery.

287
00:25:40.357 --> 00:25:45.357
And I'm going to do my duty in helping
to exact the full penalty for your crime.

288
00:25:47.237 --> 00:25:50.077
I'm sorry, Sheriff,
but it had to be your son.

289
00:25:50.977 --> 00:25:52.017
It's all right.

290
00:26:18.677 --> 00:26:20.657
I'm sorry, Benton.

291
00:26:21.677 --> 00:26:22.677
That's all right.

292
00:26:25.737 --> 00:26:27.597
I know just how you feel.

293
00:26:29.497 --> 00:26:32.144
Here's the rest of the
bank's money, Sheriff.

294
00:26:46.157 --> 00:26:48.804
Never keep me caged up
in one of them things.

295
00:26:53.117 --> 00:26:56.797
It's a mighty good thing you're out,
because Betty's home waiting for you.

296
00:26:56.877 --> 00:26:59.777
Betty was jumping to the hospital.

297
00:26:59.857 --> 00:27:02.033
And maybe you think I wasn't worried.

298
00:27:04.697 --> 00:27:05.757
Riley!

299
00:27:05.957 --> 00:27:06.917
Betty!

300
00:27:06.997 --> 00:27:09.677
Well, well, well, well.

301
00:27:12.137 --> 00:27:13.837
Never going to see you.

302
00:27:13.917 --> 00:27:17.957
Not so myself for a while,
but thanks to Jerry, here I am.

303
00:27:18.037 --> 00:27:19.577
Dinner all ready for you.

304
00:27:19.657 --> 00:27:22.217
Yeah, and I'm sure ready for dinner.

305
00:27:24.897 --> 00:27:27.777
Frank Cracky, that's the
best dinner I've had in years.

306
00:27:27.857 --> 00:27:29.397
And that goes for me, too.

307
00:27:29.477 --> 00:27:32.317
Well, I can see it isn't going
to be very hard to please you two.

308
00:27:32.397 --> 00:27:35.477
Well, son, we won't be working
the mine again the next spring.

309
00:27:35.557 --> 00:27:38.537
You know, we can't afford
to miss meals like this.

310
00:27:38.617 --> 00:27:41.735
I think I'll go out tomorrow
and hide the sluice box.

311
00:27:41.937 --> 00:27:46.197
In fact, I'll stake out three claims
along the creek, and you can file on them.

312
00:27:46.277 --> 00:27:47.857
After all, you know,

313
00:27:48.057 --> 00:27:49.857
better be on the safe side.

314
00:27:49.937 --> 00:27:53.657
And while you're gone, I'll take Betty
around the ranch and shore the town and our

315
00:27:53.737 --> 00:27:57.197
blacksmiths. Sure. And you can
figure on me being here for dinner.

316
00:27:57.277 --> 00:27:58.657
All right, Randy.

317
00:28:01.137 --> 00:28:05.237
This town is located about
six miles off that spur.

318
00:28:09.297 --> 00:28:12.017
Hey, Mason, can I see you a minute?

319
00:28:12.437 --> 00:28:14.077
Pardon me a moment, Betty.

320
00:28:21.997 --> 00:28:25.017
You know they're taking young
Miller over to Cedar City?

321
00:28:25.097 --> 00:28:29.497
Is that so? Yeah, and I thought you might
like to know that Banker William is gonna

322
00:28:29.577 --> 00:28:32.237
pull through okay.
Well, that is good news.

323
00:28:32.317 --> 00:28:33.317
Yeah.

324
00:28:40.837 --> 00:28:42.777
Is Jake Benson around?

325
00:28:42.857 --> 00:28:45.617
Why, no. He went to
his plane this morning.

326
00:28:45.697 --> 00:28:47.817
But he'll be back this afternoon.

327
00:28:48.257 --> 00:28:49.257
Oh.

328
00:28:49.917 --> 00:28:50.917
Thanks.

329
00:28:57.597 --> 00:29:00.417
Benson's out at his claim and he
won't be back till late this afternoon.

330
00:29:00.497 --> 00:29:02.909
This is just what we've been waiting for.

331
00:29:16.497 --> 00:29:17.497
Freddy?

332
00:29:18.417 --> 00:29:22.597
There's some nuggets that
Jerry don't know nothing about.

333
00:29:23.437 --> 00:29:26.597
Won't he and Betty be
surprised when they hear that?

334
00:29:32.257 --> 00:29:33.717
Come on, Friday.

335
00:30:07.657 --> 00:30:09.937
I guess we got here just in time.

336
00:30:25.457 --> 00:30:27.177
Drop your hands Benson

337
00:30:27.457 --> 00:30:32.297
We've decided it's about time you were
tipping us off to this gold field of yours So

338
00:30:32.377 --> 00:30:33.897
that's your game, eh?

339
00:30:34.077 --> 00:30:38.937
Well, Jerry and me found that gold
field We ain't tipping it off to nobody

340
00:30:52.437 --> 00:30:54.737
He's done for. Yeah.

341
00:30:54.877 --> 00:30:56.757
There's a canteen on that patch.

342
00:30:56.837 --> 00:30:59.072
Come on, we've got to catch that mule.

343
00:31:22.157 --> 00:31:24.597
Here's the canteen sure enough.

344
00:31:38.437 --> 00:31:39.437
Come on.

345
00:32:09.037 --> 00:32:10.357
Get him off!

346
00:32:32.057 --> 00:32:33.197
No use, Harris.

347
00:32:33.277 --> 00:32:36.397
I can't get it. Come on, we've got to
get out of here and get back to town.

348
00:32:36.477 --> 00:32:38.359
We can't afford to be seen here.

349
00:32:42.977 --> 00:32:45.017
I want you to go get Jerry.

350
00:32:45.097 --> 00:32:46.237
You understand?

351
00:32:46.717 --> 00:32:48.557
Go get Jerry.

352
00:32:48.637 --> 00:32:49.937
Go get him.

353
00:33:16.797 --> 00:33:18.577
Come on.

354
00:33:20.137 --> 00:33:21.177
Come on.

355
00:33:28.277 --> 00:33:30.317
Why, that's Randy's boss, isn't it?

356
00:33:30.397 --> 00:33:31.777
It sure is.

357
00:33:31.857 --> 00:33:33.457
Here comes his back.

358
00:33:33.537 --> 00:33:34.537
Yeah?

359
00:33:35.177 --> 00:33:37.077
He's ready to go back now.

360
00:33:37.157 --> 00:33:38.157
Hey.

361
00:33:39.157 --> 00:33:40.177
Hey.

362
00:33:41.297 --> 00:33:43.497
What do you suppose has happened?

363
00:33:43.837 --> 00:33:46.357
I don't know, but I'm gonna find out.

364
00:33:46.637 --> 00:33:49.857
I think there's a letter to Newtler.

365
00:33:51.677 --> 00:33:53.357
What's all the excitement about?

366
00:33:53.437 --> 00:33:56.657
Why, old Jake Horst and
Frank came in with Artie.

367
00:33:56.737 --> 00:33:58.117
Is that so? Yes.

368
00:33:58.677 --> 00:34:02.277
They made me order a
potty and a squat and...

369
00:34:02.357 --> 00:34:03.357
Yes.

370
00:34:03.697 --> 00:34:05.777
He never did this before.

371
00:34:08.657 --> 00:34:09.457
Friday!

372
00:34:09.537 --> 00:34:10.655
I'm gonna find out.

373
00:34:12.237 --> 00:34:13.757
Friday! Where's Jake?

374
00:34:19.577 --> 00:34:22.257
You better go back home and wait
till you hear from me, Betty.

375
00:34:22.337 --> 00:34:23.477
All right, Jerry.

376
00:34:52.077 --> 00:34:53.837
Thank you.

377
00:35:25.837 --> 00:35:29.037
I'm getting better every minute.

378
00:35:29.117 --> 00:35:30.317
They only nick me.

379
00:35:30.397 --> 00:35:32.077
What are you talking about?

380
00:35:32.157 --> 00:35:35.577
Who nicked you? I'll tell you
all about it on the way home.

381
00:35:35.657 --> 00:35:36.657
Come on.

382
00:35:47.877 --> 00:35:50.417
Remember now, son, not a word to Betty.

383
00:36:02.257 --> 00:36:04.057
What happened, Granby?

384
00:36:04.177 --> 00:36:07.477
Oh, you're hurt. Oh, king, nothing tall.

385
00:36:07.557 --> 00:36:09.757
Horse rode me a little square on my head.

386
00:36:09.837 --> 00:36:11.557
What I need is good feed.

387
00:36:11.637 --> 00:36:14.717
Oh, well, I'll run right up town
and get you something nice then.

388
00:36:14.797 --> 00:36:17.737
Well, don't tell anyone
that your granddad is here.

389
00:36:17.817 --> 00:36:19.217
All right.

390
00:36:24.917 --> 00:36:27.917
Hey, son, open up that trunk
and get out my makeup case,

391
00:36:27.997 --> 00:36:28.597
will you?

392
00:36:28.677 --> 00:36:30.477
Makeup case? Yeah.

393
00:36:32.477 --> 00:36:34.277
This? That's right.

394
00:36:36.497 --> 00:36:38.457
This here will stop it bleeding.

395
00:36:39.377 --> 00:36:41.297
What in the world's this?

396
00:36:41.497 --> 00:36:42.497
Oh,

397
00:36:42.857 --> 00:36:45.957
that's just a souvenir
of my old theatrical days.

398
00:36:46.177 --> 00:36:48.397
I didn't know you were an actor, Jake.

399
00:36:48.477 --> 00:36:49.417
Yep.

400
00:36:49.497 --> 00:36:53.097
I wore that when I played in
a show called Charlie's Ant.

401
00:36:53.177 --> 00:36:53.917
Yeah?

402
00:36:53.997 --> 00:36:54.997
Yeah.

403
00:36:55.377 --> 00:36:57.317
Well, what the heck is this?

404
00:36:57.397 --> 00:36:58.417
Son,

405
00:36:58.937 --> 00:37:02.737
that's the thing that helped make
Anna Held and Lillian Russell famous.

406
00:37:02.817 --> 00:37:05.157
Oh, I see. Up here like this, eh?

407
00:37:05.237 --> 00:37:06.117
No!

408
00:37:06.197 --> 00:37:10.317
Ha, ha! You darn yearling,
you got it in the wrong spot.

409
00:37:33.617 --> 00:37:36.557
I'll find out when we can
take possession of this ranch.

410
00:37:36.637 --> 00:37:37.997
Take possession?

411
00:37:38.417 --> 00:37:40.037
I don't understand.

412
00:37:40.537 --> 00:37:45.417
Well, maybe Benson didn't tell you,
but we bought this ranch a few days ago.

413
00:37:46.157 --> 00:37:47.477
That's strange.

414
00:37:47.737 --> 00:37:49.397
Funny you didn't tell me.

415
00:37:49.717 --> 00:37:51.177
You got a bill of sale?

416
00:37:51.257 --> 00:37:52.697
Why, certainly.

417
00:37:52.777 --> 00:37:53.857
It's the office.

418
00:37:54.337 --> 00:37:58.297
Well, then I'll have Jake drop in tomorrow,
and he can advise you when he's getting

419
00:37:58.377 --> 00:37:59.177
out.

420
00:37:59.257 --> 00:38:03.081
That'll be fine. We're anxious
to get started on the improvements

421
00:38:16.417 --> 00:38:17.617
What are they talking about?

422
00:38:17.697 --> 00:38:20.317
I ain't sold no ranch. Have
you signed any papers lately,

423
00:38:20.397 --> 00:38:21.597
Jake? No.

424
00:38:21.877 --> 00:38:23.057
I don't think so.

425
00:38:23.137 --> 00:38:24.757
Wait a minute. Yes, I did.

426
00:38:24.837 --> 00:38:27.737
I signed a receipt for the money
we got for them last nuggets.

427
00:38:27.817 --> 00:38:29.137
Well, did you look at it closely?

428
00:38:29.217 --> 00:38:30.217
No.

429
00:38:30.357 --> 00:38:33.217
Now, that's it, then. You probably
signed a bill of sale for the ranch.

430
00:38:33.297 --> 00:38:35.577
Oh, my God. That's why they
were trying to get rid of you.

431
00:38:35.657 --> 00:38:38.377
They figured they could claim the
ranch then and nobody could deny it.

432
00:38:38.457 --> 00:38:41.377
That dirty, low-down polecats.

433
00:38:41.457 --> 00:38:44.657
But we'll get them. You wait till
my headache's better tomorrow.

434
00:38:44.737 --> 00:38:46.897
We'll give them the
surprise of their life.

435
00:38:46.977 --> 00:38:49.506
Hey, but you better
go file on them claims.

436
00:38:49.737 --> 00:38:53.502
Take that canteen of nuggets and
leave it at the bank this time.

437
00:39:03.337 --> 00:39:05.317
Here's the location of them three claims.

438
00:39:05.397 --> 00:39:08.417
Now, there's one for Betty,
one for you, and one for me.

439
00:39:08.497 --> 00:39:09.497
All right.

440
00:39:09.597 --> 00:39:11.517
You better lie down and
get some sleep, Jake.

441
00:39:11.597 --> 00:39:13.117
Don't you forget yourself.

442
00:39:13.197 --> 00:39:14.817
Remember, I'm supposed to be dead.

443
00:39:14.897 --> 00:39:16.437
Oh, I ain't forgetting.

444
00:39:48.617 --> 00:39:50.077
There's Mason.

445
00:39:58.557 --> 00:40:01.217
Isn't that old Jake's
canteen on the saddle?

446
00:40:01.577 --> 00:40:03.197
Let's go see.

447
00:40:19.937 --> 00:40:23.349
We must have taken it off the
borough before we got there.

448
00:40:41.397 --> 00:40:42.657
How did we get there, boys?

449
00:40:42.737 --> 00:40:43.957
Oh, hello, hello. I...

450
00:40:44.037 --> 00:40:47.657
You see, Sheriff, will
you recognize this canteen?

451
00:40:47.737 --> 00:40:50.457
It belongs to old Jake Benson.

452
00:40:50.877 --> 00:40:54.017
Whenever Jake brought in his nuggets
to us, unknown to anyone else,

453
00:40:54.097 --> 00:40:55.979
he brought them in this canteen.

454
00:40:56.217 --> 00:41:01.517
And we thought it was kind of funny that
old Jake's disappeared and Mason should

455
00:41:01.597 --> 00:41:02.637
have this.

456
00:41:02.737 --> 00:41:05.657
Where is Mason? He went in the courthouse.

457
00:41:06.197 --> 00:41:08.785
But please go in and
see what Mason's doing.

458
00:41:08.937 --> 00:41:11.377
I reckon he can explain this.

459
00:41:12.317 --> 00:41:14.217
He'd better be able to.

460
00:41:29.977 --> 00:41:32.697
He's filing on a mining claim, Sheriff.

461
00:41:32.837 --> 00:41:33.897
Ah.

462
00:41:34.117 --> 00:41:36.217
Probably old Jake's claim.

463
00:41:36.777 --> 00:41:39.437
Well, we'll just wait till he gets here.

464
00:41:46.797 --> 00:41:48.157
Howdy, boys.

465
00:41:48.377 --> 00:41:50.297
What's all the pow-wow about?

466
00:41:50.557 --> 00:41:53.857
Just how did you come to
have this cantina's nugget?

467
00:41:54.037 --> 00:41:56.837
I don't care to answer
that question, Harris.

468
00:41:57.617 --> 00:42:00.277
Whose claim are you just filing on, Mason?

469
00:42:00.437 --> 00:42:02.057
My own claim.

470
00:42:02.697 --> 00:42:05.237
Do you know anything about
Jake Benson's disappearance?

471
00:42:05.317 --> 00:42:07.417
Yes, I know he hasn't come back.

472
00:42:07.937 --> 00:42:11.996
I'm sorry, Mason, but I'll have to
hold you until we can locate Jake.

473
00:42:12.957 --> 00:42:14.437
That's fair enough.

474
00:42:14.517 --> 00:42:16.693
When do I get my preliminary hearing?

475
00:42:17.117 --> 00:42:18.837
First thing tomorrow morning.

476
00:42:19.977 --> 00:42:22.859
You better take charge
of those nuggets, Sheriff.

477
00:42:43.677 --> 00:42:45.383
What are they gonna do to me?

478
00:42:48.717 --> 00:42:50.497
What's happened? What's wrong?

479
00:42:50.577 --> 00:42:52.017
Mason's up for murder.

480
00:42:52.157 --> 00:42:52.857
Murder?

481
00:42:52.937 --> 00:42:53.937
Yes.

482
00:43:03.077 --> 00:43:05.557
Mr. Taylor, may I
please have a moment, Mr.

483
00:43:05.637 --> 00:43:06.597
Mason?

484
00:43:06.677 --> 00:43:08.157
Yes, I guess so.

485
00:43:08.237 --> 00:43:10.017
Go ahead. Thank you.

486
00:43:12.237 --> 00:43:14.157
Oh, Jerry. Now listen, Betty.

487
00:43:14.237 --> 00:43:16.531
They think I've murdered your granddad.

488
00:43:16.657 --> 00:43:19.557
I'm not saying anything to anyone, but
hurry home and tell Jake that I have a

489
00:43:19.637 --> 00:43:21.177
preliminary hearing in the morning.

490
00:43:21.257 --> 00:43:23.897
And for him to get there
without being seen by anyone.

491
00:43:23.977 --> 00:43:25.097
All right, Jake.

492
00:43:25.417 --> 00:43:26.417
Goodbye.

493
00:43:28.937 --> 00:43:29.937
Goodbye.

494
00:44:06.257 --> 00:44:07.717
I understand.

495
00:44:07.937 --> 00:44:09.037
Yes.

496
00:44:09.277 --> 00:44:10.497
Will I be there?

497
00:44:10.577 --> 00:44:12.197
And how?

498
00:44:15.617 --> 00:44:17.957
We figured out the way I said.

499
00:44:18.037 --> 00:44:20.057
Captain Chant, nor Louie.

500
00:44:21.537 --> 00:44:23.517
We'll be getting out of here.

501
00:44:23.597 --> 00:44:25.303
It's going to help the world.

502
00:44:33.597 --> 00:44:36.837
Pardon me, gentlemen, but I'm
looking for the courthouse.

503
00:44:36.917 --> 00:44:38.976
You're standing right in it, madam.

504
00:44:39.877 --> 00:44:42.057
Oh, for goodness sake.

505
00:44:42.157 --> 00:44:44.997
I do love murder trials, don't you?

506
00:44:45.377 --> 00:44:49.677
But if I were a murderer, I'd much prefer
the electric chair than to have a rope

507
00:44:49.757 --> 00:44:51.637
around my neck, wouldn't you?

508
00:44:51.717 --> 00:44:54.257
Listen, lady, we're not interested.

509
00:44:54.917 --> 00:44:56.717
But you're going to be.

510
00:45:00.837 --> 00:45:03.457
Well, here comes the
sheriff and Mason now.

511
00:45:05.537 --> 00:45:08.017
My goodness, what big things!

512
00:45:11.997 --> 00:45:14.409
Just a minute, boys. Check your hardware.

513
00:45:27.997 --> 00:45:29.157
Come on, let's get in here.

514
00:45:29.237 --> 00:45:31.237
This thing is just about to start.

515
00:45:54.197 --> 00:45:55.477
Thank you.

516
00:46:33.697 --> 00:46:35.657
Hear ye, hear ye, hear ye.

517
00:46:35.737 --> 00:46:37.817
The Court of Sonoma,
Howe County is now open.

518
00:46:37.897 --> 00:46:39.317
Judge McGill for his ID.

519
00:46:39.397 --> 00:46:42.221
Everybody be seated and
come to immediate order.

520
00:46:48.377 --> 00:46:49.577
Your Honor,

521
00:46:50.117 --> 00:46:54.117
before you proceed further with this case,
there's a few words I'd like to say.

522
00:46:54.197 --> 00:46:55.977
What is your name, madam?

523
00:46:56.317 --> 00:46:58.257
Veronica Mehippo Benson.

524
00:46:58.677 --> 00:47:00.357
Any relation to Jake Benson?

525
00:47:00.437 --> 00:47:01.377
Oh, yes.

526
00:47:01.457 --> 00:47:03.077
I'm his nearest relative.

527
00:47:03.697 --> 00:47:05.117
What do you want to say, madam?

528
00:47:05.197 --> 00:47:09.917
I wanted to say that I've known the
accused since he was a babe in arms.

529
00:47:15.597 --> 00:47:17.077
Why, uh, please?

530
00:47:17.157 --> 00:47:24.097
As I was about to say, I knew him years
ago, and he was the sweetest thing.

531
00:47:29.537 --> 00:47:34.677
Come to the point, madam. Well,
I know who shot Jake Benson.

532
00:47:35.657 --> 00:47:40.397
The men are in this court, Your Honor,
and I advise the sheriff not to let anyone

533
00:47:40.477 --> 00:47:41.877
leave this room.

534
00:47:44.397 --> 00:47:46.557
They tried to steal his mind.

535
00:47:46.677 --> 00:47:48.737
They tried to steal his ranch.

536
00:47:48.817 --> 00:47:52.097
And they shot him down in cold blood.

537
00:47:52.437 --> 00:47:54.497
How do you know this, madam?

538
00:47:54.577 --> 00:47:57.459
Because I was there when
it happened, Your Honor.

539
00:48:07.357 --> 00:48:10.257
Sheriff, try to miss Benson then.

540
00:48:14.437 --> 00:48:16.217
Order in the cross!

541
00:48:16.297 --> 00:48:17.297
Order!

542
00:48:20.737 --> 00:48:21.877
Lady!

543
00:48:21.957 --> 00:48:23.737
Put down your dress!

544
00:48:23.817 --> 00:48:26.977
I ain't no lady. I'm Jake Benson.

545
00:48:27.057 --> 00:48:29.777
And there's the two coyotes that shot me.

546
00:48:29.857 --> 00:48:31.739
I'm not a lady. I'm Jake Benson.

547
00:48:53.177 --> 00:48:54.677
There he goes!

548
00:49:04.137 --> 00:49:05.877
Why not switch, Mick?

549
00:49:05.957 --> 00:49:07.857
How do you run this darn thing?

550
00:49:07.937 --> 00:49:09.237
I'll do the driver.

551
00:49:51.537 --> 00:49:54.917
There we go.

552
00:50:32.997 --> 00:50:36.317
Oh, my God.

553
00:50:53.397 --> 00:50:56.197
I'm sorry.

554
00:51:23.917 --> 00:51:24.917
Come on.

555
00:52:19.357 --> 00:52:21.717
I'm sorry.

556
00:52:59.057 --> 00:53:00.337
Thank you.

557
00:53:40.277 --> 00:53:42.457
All right now, folks, that looks fine.

558
00:53:42.537 --> 00:53:44.437
Now, just a minute. Relax for a minute.

559
00:53:44.517 --> 00:53:45.797
Now, here we go.

560
00:53:46.157 --> 00:53:49.957
You must remember that I spent most all
of the afternoon trying to get you in

561
00:53:50.037 --> 00:53:50.797
position.

562
00:53:50.877 --> 00:53:51.797
Now, hold it.

563
00:53:51.877 --> 00:53:53.357
Just like that.

564
00:53:53.877 --> 00:53:55.237
Still, hold it.

565
00:53:55.377 --> 00:53:56.517
Hold it!

566
00:53:58.697 --> 00:54:00.557
Ready now.

